Follow these steps to get the specific credentials you need for your GitHub Secrets.
Phase 1: Get your Client ID and Secret
 * Go to the Google Cloud Console.
 * Enable the API: Search for "YouTube Data API v3" and click Enable.
 * OAuth Consent Screen: * Set User Type to External.
   * Crucial: Add your own email address to the "Test Users" list.
 * Create Credentials: * Go to Credentials > Create Credentials > OAuth client ID.
   * Select Desktop app as the application type.
   * Download the resulting JSON file and rename it to credentials.json.
Phase 2: Get your Refresh Token (The "Missing Link")
Since GitHub Actions cannot "click" a login button, you must generate the refresh token on your own computer first.
1. Install the tools:
Open your computer's terminal (or command prompt) and run:
pip install --upgrade google-api-python-client google-auth-httplib2 google-auth-oauthlib

2. Run this "Token Maker" script:
Create a file named get_token.py in the same folder as your credentials.json and paste this:
from google_auth_oauthlib.flow import InstalledAppFlow

# The scope for uploading to YouTube
SCOPES = ['https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.upload']

def get_refresh_token():
    flow = InstalledAppFlow.from_client_secrets_file('credentials.json', SCOPES)
    # This will open a browser window for you to log in
    creds = flow.run_local_server(port=0)
    
    print("\n✅ Success! Copy these three values into your GitHub Secrets:")
    print(f"CLIENT_ID: {creds.client_id}")
    print(f"CLIENT_SECRET: {creds.client_secret}")
    print(f"REFRESH_TOKEN: {creds.refresh_token}")

if __name__ == '__main__':
    get_refresh_token()

3. Execute: Run python get_token.py. A browser will open; log in with the account for @Risedailynow2. The script will then print your Refresh Token in the terminal.
Phase 3: Secure your GitHub Repo
Now that you have the three values, go to your Risedailynow2 repository on GitHub:
 * Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions.
 * Add these New repository secrets:
   * YOUTUBE_CLIENT_ID
